ing our licenses, and could also result in a suspension or revocation of these licenses.","context":"Our manufacturing facility in North Carolina is integral to our tobacco business. Adverse changes or developments affecting this facility, including, but not limited to, disease or infestation of our raw materials, a fire, an explosion, a serious injury or fatality, a power failure, a natural disaster, an epidemic, pandemic or other public health crisis, or a material failure of our security infrastructure, could reduce or require us to entirely suspend operations.","section":"We may become subject to litigation related to cigarette smoking and/or exposure to environmental tobacco smoke, or ETS, which could severely impair our results of operations and liquidity.","block":221,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-034814","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-03-26","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001347858","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1347858/000110465926034814/xxii-20251231x10k.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/36ab0b783879335128ceaf91dbdf8885b06e6d6b56888205473e95185abd7f7d.bin","sha256":"36ab0b783879335128ceaf91dbdf8885b06e6d6b56888205473e95185abd7f7d"}},{"id":"37a5ccbd6f59b7fb063aa77753b5304c75db3f9e109905f22508d4b0455e86c1","quote":"The loss of a significant customer for whom we manufacture tobacco products could have an adverse impact on our results of operation.","context":"16","section":"We may become subject to litigation related to cigarette smoking and/or exposure to environmental tobacco smoke, or ETS, which could severely impair our results of operations and liquidity.","block":223,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-034814","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-03-26","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001347858","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1347858/000110465926034814/xxii-20251231x10k.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/36ab0b783879335128ceaf91dbdf8885b06e6d6b56888205473e95185abd7f7d.bin","sha256":"36ab0b783879335128ceaf91dbdf8885b06e6d6b56888205473e95185abd7f7d"}},{"id":"6130a136f961e1062393e6b3e42d93c23dfa5d3b0342f805f5c425901005d8de","quote":"Currently, a significant portion of our revenues (and corresponding accounts receivable) from manufacturing tobacco products are derived from a small number of large customers, and we do not have agreements with such customers requiring them to purchase a minimum amount of products from us or guaranteeing any minimum future purchase amounts from us. Such customers may, at any time, delay or decrease their level of purchases from us or cease doing business with us altogether. Since many of our manufacturing costs are fixed, if sales to such customers cease or are reduced, we may not obtain sufficient purchase orders from other customers necessary to offset any such losses or reductions, which could have a negative impact on our results of operations.","context":"The loss of a significant customer for whom we manufacture tobacco products could have an adverse impact on our results of operation.","section":"We may become subject to litigation related to cigarette smoking and/or exposure to environmental tobacco smoke, or ETS, which could severely impair our results of operations and liquidity.","block":224,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-034814","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-03-26","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001347858","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1347858/000110465926034814/xxii-20251231x10k.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/36ab0b783879335128ceaf91dbdf8885b06e6d6b56888205473e95185abd7f7d.bin","sha256":"36ab0b783879335128ceaf91dbdf8885b06e6d6b56888205473e95185abd7f7d"}},{"id":"6a656da0f6c0c9399dde49e9082f3c383736490cadeb127fd3119b79af8f6d9c","quote":"Product liability claims, product recalls, or other claims could cause us to incur losses or damage our reputation.","context":"Currently, a significant portion of our revenues (and corresponding accounts receivable) from manufacturing tobacco products are derived from a small number of large customers, and we do not have agreements with such customers requiring them to purchase a minimum amount of products from us or guaranteeing any minimum future purchase amounts from us. Such customers may, at any time, delay or decrease their level of purchases from us or cease doing business with us altogether. Since many of our manufacturing costs are fixed, if sales to such customers cease or are reduced, we may not obtain sufficient purchase orders from other customers necessary to offset any such losses or reductions, which could have a negative impact on our results of operations.","section":"We may become subject to litigation related to cigarette smoking and/or exposure to environmental tobacco smoke, or ETS, which could severely impair our results of operations and liquidity.","block":225,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-034814","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-03-26","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001347858","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1347858/000110465926034814/xxii-20251231x10k.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/36ab0b783879335128ceaf91dbdf8885b06e6d6b56888205473e95185abd7f7d.bin","sha256":"36ab0b783879335128ceaf91dbdf8885b06e6d6b56888205473e95185abd7f7d"}},{"id":"82487f6607f40d7c21053e4e6e2f1343c2b1af11b0eea46c3c05892b56e465db","quote":"The risk of product liability claims, product recalls, and associated adverse publicity, is inherent in the development, manufacturing, marketing, and sale of tobacco products. Any product recall or lawsuit seeking significant monetary damages may have a material adverse effect on our business and financial condition. A successful product liability claim against us could require us to pay a substantial monetary award. Though we currently have no pending product liability claims against us, we cannot assure you that such claims will not be made in the future and any such claim could cause us to incur substantial losses or damage our reputation.","context":"Product liability claims, product recalls, or other claims could cause us to incur losses or damage our reputation.","section":"We may become subject to litigation related to cigarette smoking and/or exposure to environmental tobacco smoke, or ETS, which could severely impair our results of operations and liquidity.","block":226,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-034814","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-03-26","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001347858","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1347858/000110465926034814/xxii-20251231x10k.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/36ab0b783879335128ceaf91dbdf8885b06e6d6b56888205473e95185abd7f7d.bin","sha256":"36ab0b783879335128ceaf91dbdf8885b06e6d6b56888205473e95185abd7f7d"}},{"id":"86c4b2811036febed0e0ff61128ced408e2dde272194a933f4c4d1d3683967e3","quote":"Cigarettes are subject to substantial taxes. Significant increases in cigarette-related taxes have been proposed or enacted and are likely to continue to be proposed or enacted in numerous jurisdictions. These tax increases may affect the sales of our potential products and our third-parties customers’ tobacco products manufactured at our factory, which could result in decreased sales and profitability of our manufacturing business.","context":"The risk of product liability claims, product recalls, and associated adverse publicity, is inherent in the development, manufacturing, marketing, and sale of tobacco products. Any product recall or lawsuit seeking significant monetary damages may have a material adverse effect on our business and financial condition. A successful product liability claim against us could require us to pay a substantial monetary award. Though we currently have no pending product liability claims against us, we cannot assure you that such claims will not be made in the future and any such claim could cause us to incur substantial losses or damage our reputation.","section":"We may become subject to litigation related to cigarette smoking and/or exposure to environmental tobacco smoke, or ETS, which could severely impair our results of operations and liquidity.","block":227,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-034814","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-03-26","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001347858","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1347858/000110465926034814/xxii-20251231x10k.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/36ab0b783879335128ceaf91dbdf8885b06e6d6b56888205473e95185abd7f7d.bin","sha256":"36ab0b783879335128ceaf91dbdf8885b06e6d6b56888205473e95185abd7f7d"}},{"id":"f5806d2b3f86f15898f8fbac7e18ecfb04f16f3e6400460c5752b7cadb493bcb","quote":"Tax regimes, including excise taxes, sales taxes, and import duties, can disproportionately affect the retail price of manufactured cigarettes versus other tobacco products, or disproportionately affect the relative retail price of our Modified Exposure Cigarettes versus lower-priced cigarette brands manufactured by our competitors. Increases in cigarette taxes are expected to continue to have an adverse impact on sales of cigarettes resulting in (i) lower consumption levels, (ii) a shift in sales from manufactured cigarettes to other tobacco products or to lower-price cigarette categories, (iii) a shift from local sales to legal cross-border purchases of lower price products, and (iv) illicit products such as contraband and counterfeit.","context":"Cigarettes are subject to substantial taxes. Significant increases in cigarette-related taxes have been proposed or enacted and are likely to continue to be proposed or enacted in numerous jurisdictions. These tax increases may affect the sales of our potential products and our third-parties customers’ tobacco products manufactured at our factory, which could result in decreased sales and profitability of our manufacturing business.","section":"We may become subject to litigation related to cigarette smoking and/or exposure to environmental tobacco smoke, or ETS, which could severely impair our results of operations and liquidity.","block":228,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-034814","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-03-26","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001347858","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1347858/000110465926034814/xxii-20251231x10k.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/36ab0b783879335128ceaf91dbdf8885b06e6d6b56888205473e95185abd7f7d.bin","sha256":"36ab0b783879335128ceaf91dbdf8885b06e6d6b56888205473e95185abd7f7d"}},{"id":"22538949e7dc7d782c9447981d4a614b2ffdec3516fc8fcb967e5aaa3b4d3f51","quote":"Government mandated prices or taxes, production control programs, shifts in crops driven by economic conditions, climatic or adverse weather patterns may increase the cost or reduce the quality and/or supply of the tobacco and other agricultural products used to manufacture our products.","context":"Tax regimes, including excise taxes, sales taxes, and import duties, can disproportionately affect the retail price of manufactured cigarettes versus other tobacco products, or disproportionately affect the relative retail price of our Modified Exposure Cigarettes versus lower-priced cigarette brands manufactured by our competitors. Increases in cigarette taxes are expected to continue to have an adverse impact on sales of cigarettes resulting in (i) lower consumption levels, (ii) a shift in sales from manufactured cigarettes to other tobacco products or to lower-price cigarette categories, (iii) a shift from local sales to legal cross-border purchases of lower price products, and (iv) illicit products such as contraband and counterfeit.","section":"We may become subject to litigation related to cigarette smoking and/or exposure to environmental tobacco smoke, or ETS, which could severely impair our results of operations and liquidity.","block":229,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-034814","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-03-26","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001347858","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1347858/000110465926034814/xxii-20251231x10k.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/36ab0b783879335128ceaf91dbdf8885b06e6d6b56888205473e95185abd7f7d.bin","sha256":"36ab0b783879335128ceaf91dbdf8885b06e6d6b56888205473e95185abd7f7d"}},{"id":"4b911aeaae97aa9380cf4b62f3cab1a234fe050d6629290c0353c23df6742d88","quote":"We depend on a small number of independent tobacco farmers to grow our specialty proprietary tobaccos with specific nicotine contents for our products. As with other agricultural commodities, the price of tobacco leaf can be influenced by imbalances in supply and demand, and crop quality can be influenced by variations in weather patterns, diseases, and pests. This risk is greater for us, as there would be no alternative supply of RNC tobacco in the event that one of our growers experiences a material adverse event, such as a natural disaster, with respect to a particular RNC tobacco crop or the quantity or quality was not as we anticipated, and we would not be able to supply leaf for our VLN® cigarettes.","context":"Government mandated prices or taxes, production control programs, shifts in crops driven by economic conditions, climatic or adverse weather patterns may increase the cost or reduce the quality and/or supply of the tobacco and other agricultural products used to manufacture our products.","section":"We may become subject to litigation related to cigarette smoking and/or exposure to environmental tobacco smoke, or ETS, which could severely impair our results of operations and liquidity.","block":230,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-034814","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-03-26","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001347858","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1347858/000110465926034814/xxii-20251231x10k.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/36ab0b783879335128ceaf91dbdf8885b06e6d6b56888205473e95185abd7f7d.bin","sha256":"36ab0b783879335128ceaf91dbdf8885b06e6d6b56888205473e95185abd7f7d"}},{"id":"07704434df5a39579d792287f8b4bdd77949b80b680ed04769101f3f5abd4f83","quote":"We must also compete with other tobacco companies for contract production with independent tobacco farmers. Tobacco production in certain countries is subject to a variety of controls, including government mandated prices and production control programs. Changes in the patterns of demand for agricultural products could cause farmers to plant less tobacco. Any significant change in tobacco leaf prices or taxes, quality and quantity could affect our profitability and our business.","context":"We depend on a small number of independent tobacco farmers to grow our specialty proprietary tobaccos with specific nicotine contents for our products. As with other agricultural commodities, the price of tobacco leaf can be influenced by imbalances in supply and demand, and crop quality can be influenced by variations in weather patterns, diseases, and pests. This risk is greater for us, as there would be no alternative supply of RNC tobacco in the event that one of our growers experiences a material adverse event, such as a natural disaster, with respect to a particular RNC tobacco crop or the quantity or quality was not as we anticipated, and we would not be able to supply leaf for our VLN® cigarettes.","section":"We may become subject to litigation related to cigarette smoking and/or exposure to environmental tobacco smoke, or ETS, which could severely impair our results of operations and liquidity.","block":231,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-034814","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-03-26","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001347858","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1347858/000110465926034814/xxii-20251231x10k.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/36ab0b783879335128ceaf91dbdf8885b06e6d6b56888205473e95185abd7f7d.bin","sha256":"36ab0b783879335128ceaf91dbdf8885b06e6d6b56888205473e95185abd7f7d"}},{"id":"6c7275794484a6853cc1465965dc0a77ae7f326eaf2e899f1a92e18e2530c2bb","quote":"We may distribute and sell our products outside of the U.S., which subjects us to other regulatory risks.","context":"17","section":"We may become subject to litigation related to cigarette smoking and/or exposure to environmental tobacco smoke, or ETS, which could severely impair our results of operations and liquidity.","block":233,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-034814","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-03-26","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001347858","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1347858/000110465926034814/xxii-20251231x10k.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/36ab0b783879335128ceaf91dbdf8885b06e6d6b56888205473e95185abd7f7d.bin","sha256":"36ab0b783879335128ceaf91dbdf8885b06e6d6b56888205473e95185abd7f7d"}},{"id":"6ccd96436860f4a5cdf64c6107c8973a6d0e0871bfd901973652e8586c15cc2f","quote":"We may seek governmental authorizations required to market our RNC tobacco cigarettes and our other products in other countries. Marketing of our products is not permitted in certain countries until we have obtained required authorizations or exemptions in these individual countries. The regulatory review process varies from country to country, and authorization by foreign governmental authorities is unpredictable, uncertain, and generally expensive. Our ability to market our potential products could be substantially limited due to delays in receipt of, or failure to receive, the necessary authorizations or exemptions. We anticipate commencing the applications required in some or all of these countries in the future. Failure to obtain necessary regulatory authorizations or exemptions could impair our ability to generate revenue from international sources.","context":"We may distribute and sell our products outside of the U.S., which subjects us to other regulatory risks.","section":"We may become subject to litigation related to cigarette smoking and/or exposure to environmental tobacco smoke, or ETS, which could severely impair our results of operations and liquidity.","block":234,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-034814","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-03-26","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001347858","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1347858/000110465926034814/xxii-20251231x10k.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/36ab0b783879335128ceaf91dbdf8885b06e6d6b56888205473e95185abd7f7d.bin","sha256":"36ab0b783879335128ceaf91dbdf8885b06e6d6b56888205473e95185abd7f7d"}},{"id":"f1345a7315a9a814d474def8d04fae0ee0012b87bdc185ff27b94443e1b78d75","quote":"We may become subject to governmental investigations on a range of matters.","context":"We may seek governmental authorizations required to market our RNC tobacco cigarettes and our other products in other countries. Marketing of our products is not permitted in certain countries until we have obtained required authorizations or exemptions in these individual countries. The regulatory review process varies from country to country, and authorization by foreign governmental authorities is unpredictable, uncertain, and generally expensive. Our ability to market our potential products could be substantially limited due to delays in receipt of, or failure to receive, the necessary authorizations or exemptions. We anticipate commencing the applications required in some or all of these countries in the future. Failure to obtain necessary regulatory authorizations or exemptions could impair our ability to generate revenue from international sources.","section":"We may become subject to litigation related to cigarette smoking and/or exposure to environmental tobacco smoke, or ETS, which could severely impair our results of operations and liquidity.","block":235,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-034814","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-03-26","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001347858","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1347858/000110465926034814/xxii-20251231x10k.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/36ab0b783879335128ceaf91dbdf8885b06e6d6b56888205473e95185abd7f7d.bin","sha256":"36ab0b783879335128ceaf91dbdf8885b06e6d6b56888205473e95185abd7f7d"}},{"id":"82d357fe6bc94f79c8c26c300257a00112c64aeff11ec15c098a4ed0f2ef8c60","quote":"Tobacco companies are often subject to investigations, including allegations of contraband shipments of cigarettes, allegations of unlawful pricing activities within certain markets, allegations of underpayment of custom duties and/or excise taxes, and allegations of false and misleading usage of descriptors such as “lights” and “ultra-lights.” We cannot predict the outcome of any investigations to which we may become subject, but we may be materially affected by an unfavorable outcome of potential future investigations.","context":"We may become subject to governmental investigations on a range of matters.","section":"We may become subject to litigation related to cigarette smoking and/or exposure to environmental tobacco smoke, or ETS, which could severely impair our results of operations and liquidity.","block":236,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-034814","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-03-26","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001347858","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1347858/000110465926034814/xxii-20251231x10k.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/36ab0b783879335128ceaf91dbdf8885b06e6d6b56888205473e95185abd7f7d.bin","sha256":"36ab0b783879335128ceaf91dbdf8885b06e6d6b56888205473e95185abd7f7d"}},{"id":"5362b21a84e8cb52c16480f4b9f75004027e94624533dba7f1acf0f97d3d2931","quote":"We may be unsuccessful in anticipating changes in adult consumer preferences, responding to changes in consumer purchase behavior or managing through difficult competitive and economic conditions, which could have an adverse effect on business.","context":"Tobacco companies are often subject to investigations, including allegations of contraband shipments of cigarettes, allegations of unlawful pricing activities within certain markets, allegations of underpayment of custom duties and/or excise taxes, and allegations of false and misleading usage of descriptors such as “lights” and “ultra-lights.” We cannot predict the outcome of any investigations to which we may become subject, but we may be materially affected by an unfavorable outcome of potential future investigations.","section":"We may become subject to litigation related to cigarette smoking and/or exposure to environmental tobacco smoke, or ETS, which could severely impair our results of operations and liquidity.","block":237,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-034814","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-03-26","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001347858","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1347858/000110465926034814/xxii-20251231x10k.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/36ab0b783879335128ceaf91dbdf8885b06e6d6b56888205473e95185abd7f7d.